  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved 0.586 acc / 0.574 F1, substantially outperforming config_018 (scgpt, same other settings) at 0.520 acc. This strongly suggests pca_n2000 is the superior RNA encoder in this multimodal-multiprofile setup. Question: Does the fusion mechanism (weighted vs. concat) meaningfully affect performance when all other components are held at their best-known values? config_023 is the minimal single-variable change from the current best (only fusion switches from weighted to concat), directly testing whether the weighted fusion is adding value or whether a simpler concatenation is equally or more effective. Why this is the best next experiment: With only 2 data points, we need to reduce uncertainty about the remaining high-impact design choices around the promising pca_n2000+imagenet_vit_l+transformer backbone. Fusion is a core architectural decision that interacts with how the two modalities are combined, and resolving it early (with 7 experiments still remaining) lets subsequent experiments focus on image encoder or aggregation choices with a clearer picture of the optimal fusion strategy."
}

